# Single-instance-only local override file for ds-storage.
#
# IMPORTANT: if this service ever shares a Tomcat instance with other WARs (as the development server does,
# running all 6 ds-backend services in one Tomcat), do NOT use this file for devops/operations secrets such as
# the database password - use conf/ds-storage-application.properties.SAMPLE instead. The reason: this file is
# picked up via SmallRye Config's own implicit 'config/application.properties' convention (ordinal 260), keyed
# off the JVM's current working directory - which every webapp in that shared Tomcat instance has in common, so
# there is no way for this file to affect only ds-storage. A file left here would silently apply to every
# service sharing that Tomcat instance. conf/ds-storage-application.properties is instead read from an explicit,
# per-service path configured via its own Tomcat context environment entry, so it cannot leak across services.
#
# This file is only safe to use for a single, standalone instance of the service (e.g. running it alone via an
# IDE, or 'java -jar', from a working directory nothing else shares) - copy it to 'config/application.properties'
# (same folder, without the '.SAMPLE' suffix) and fill in your own values; no code change and no extra argument
# to ServiceConfig.initialize(...) is needed for it to apply, since addDefaultSources() already registers it.
#
# 'config/application.properties' is (and must stay) git-ignored; see .gitignore.
#
# Any key present in ds-storage-behaviour.yaml can be overridden here, using the same dotted path. Only the keys
# below are the ones commonly overridden per environment/operator - uncomment and set the ones you need.

# db.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/ds-storage
# db.driver=org.postgresql.Driver
# db.username=ds_storage_user
# db.password=changeme
# db.connectionPoolSize=10

# security.baseurl=https://keycloak.example.org/realms
# security.client.id=some_client
# security.client.secret=changeme

# openapi.serverurl=http://localhost:9072/ds-storage/v1
